14. AUDIO, SESSION, AND LIFECYCLE MANAGEMENT

Preserve the existing global voice assistant architecture.

Use:

- One shared VoiceAssistantViewModel.
- One shared conversation/session manager.
- One WebSocket connection manager.
- One audio recording manager.
- One audio playback manager.
- One reusable Compose assistant widget.

Do not create separate assistant sessions or ViewModels for every screen.

Interruption handling

The user must be able to interrupt AI speech by starting a new voice request where the selected Gemini API supports it.

When interrupted:

- Stop old playback immediately.
- Cancel the old response job.
- Clear stale audio buffers.
- Discard stale response chunks.
- Process the new request.
- Preserve conversation context.

Use request IDs or turn IDs to prevent stale responses from appearing.

Lifecycle

When the application enters the background:

- Stop microphone recording.
- Stop audio transmission.
- Stop AI audio playback.
- Cancel active audio operations safely.
- Preserve conversation context.
- Prevent unexpected background playback.

When the application returns to the foreground:

- Restore the assistant interface if appropriate.
- Restore conversation history.
- Check session validity.
- Reconnect when necessary.
- Do not automatically start recording.

Do not use a foreground service just to keep the assistant speaking in the background.

